{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"Shell|sprite|tones|anim|settings|menu|overhead|Path\" Attack-of-the-Timelout-Attack-of-the-Timelord-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022923/vendor/engine-repo/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md | head -100'","aggregated_output":"63:- 572 Standard features; settings, fullscreen\n66:- 611 10e. Paths; E.Path: path\n87:- 1123 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n88:- 1184 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n170:- `E.mkCanvas(w, h)`: a new canvas of w x h pixels (scratch images and sprite sheets). With no document (Node: a headless game) a stand-in whose drawing does nothing, so sprites and other images made  [... omitted end of long line]\n191:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default  [... omitted end of long line]\n197:- `E.px`: the pixel primitives: px.rect, px.line, px.dot, px.disc, px.poly, px.sprite, ... (each snaps to whole pixels)\n210:- `px.sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip = false)`: draw a sprite with its top-left corner at buffer pixel (x, y). flip mirrors it left-right; or o: { flip, rot (radians, turned about its center: E.rotSprite), [... omitted end of long line]\n211:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enla [... omitted end of long line]\n216:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprit [... omitted end of long line]\n217:- `E.recolor(spr, map)` †: a copy of a sprite with its colors swapped (palette swaps: the second player, a hurt flash, a stronger enemy): recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a', h: '#e0b040' }), each key [... omitted end of long line]\n218:- `E.rotSprite(spr, a, steps = 16)` †: the sprite turned by angle a (radians; the way the world's angles turn, so a ship drawn facing east turns to its facing): nearest-neighbour, whole pixels, about  [... omitted end of long line]\n222:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: [... omitted end of long line]\n223:- `E.VIEW_ORDER: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side`: the order game.nextView() cycles through when a game doesn't set game.views ('overhead' is left out)\n245:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n262:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.fil [... omitted end of long line]\n267:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the la [... omitted end of long line]\n276:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Inp [... omitted end of long line]\n279:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n286:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n302:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n303:- `input.rebind(a, device, code)` †: bind action a to one code for a device ('keys' = keyboard and mouse, 'pad' = gamepad), in place of that device's codes: input.rebind('attack', 'keys', 'KeyF'). Ret [... omitted end of long line]\n304:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the ga [... omitted end of long line]\n307:- `input.repeat(a, delay = .3, rate = .08)`: pressed, then repeats while held (after `delay` s, every `rate` s): menu cursors, puzzle pieces\n318:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size the [... omitted end of long line]\n321:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. E [... omitted end of long line]\n330:- `input.invertMoveX`, `input.invertMoveY = false` †: the move stick turned round (the Controller settings)\n335:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new binding [... omitted end of long line]\n345:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n415:- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background characte [... omitted end of long line]\n416:- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n429:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n430:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicke