as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom [... omitted end of long line]\n530:- `game.drawEvery = 1`: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost, or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, even [... omitted end of long line]\n541:- `game.live` †: true (o.live): a pause opens the menus over a world that keeps stepping (an online or shared world can't stop for one player): paused is true and the scene's update goes on, the menu  [... omitted end of long line]\n545:- `game.pauseReason = null`: why the game paused: 'player' | 'focus' (the page was hidden) | 'controller' (unplugged) | 'menu', or null\n554:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n555:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n568:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom ran [... omitted end of long line]\n574:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n575:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its  [... omitted end of long line]\n576:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n577:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n578:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old