})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, out [... omitted end of long line]\n1155:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: ! [... omitted end of long line]\n1156:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1157:- `menu.rowAt(i)` †: entry i's box on the screen, [x, y, w, h] in screen pixels: where a click or tap picks it (a test's feed('down') and feed('up') there); null while it is scrolled out of view\n1158:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1159:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1160:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1161:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1162:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1163:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1164:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1165:- `menu.game`: its game\n1166:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
