{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('Attack-of-the-Timelout-Attack-of-the-Timelord-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022923/docs/build-notes.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Two focused engine changes apply','Three focused engine changes apply').replace('2. Fixed-resolution Screen sizing permits fractional downscaling when the viewport is smaller than the logical canvas. The unmodified minimum1 cropped1066×600 on small screens. Native pointer mapping, letterboxing and collision coordinates now remain aligned. Default scaling is Fill.','2. Fixed-resolution Screen sizing permits fractional downscaling when the viewport is smaller than the logical canvas. The unmodified minimum1 cropped1066×600 on small screens. A rounding epsilon keeps fit margins stable. Native pointer mapping, letterboxing and collision coordinates now remain aligned. Default scaling is Fill.\\\\n3. Shell same-name refresh preserves focus before replacing its screen record. Without this, controller character pickers jumped back to the first button after every edit.').replace('The canonical world never reads DOM, draws or plays audio.','The canonical world never reads DOM, draws or plays audio. A separate monotonic network clock catches up fixed steps independently of rendering and local shell pause, and sampled input expires after350ms.');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Final verification pass in progress\n- All game features, menus, independent network clock, sticky assisted records and final credits/feedback are implemented. Root HTML rebuilt at1431KiB with final interview data; exit-interview.json synchronized.\n- State23/23, engine8/8, network18/18. Audio27/27. Browser final suite122 checks (affected49 and38 passed after last fixes). OfficialHub4/4 and real packagedWebRTC15/15 previously passed; final suite adds two input-freshness/no-render checks.\n- Independent network clock is now production behavior, not a test bypass. Local sampled input expires350ms and is cleared on focus/controller loss. Public signaling transiently timed out but real data links succeeded after retry.\n- Final quiet all-suite run currently running in exec session17834. Poll with write_stdin; logs only at end. Expected total234 if all groups complete. Correct any reported failures before delivery.\n- Final docs: README, research, authoring, build-notes, audio, network, verification. Finding ledger26 issues:10 test/visual,16 focused review;5 potentially game breaking. All fixed.\n- Contact sheet: test-artifacts/browser-contact-sheet.png/.html,12 genuine screenshots. Need refresh after final browser screenshot run if desired with tests/contact-sheet.py.\n- Remaining only: inspect all-suite result, record artifact hash/final counts, final progress update and final reply with required Source Information and all ordered feedback answers. Do not modify runtime after testing without rebuild and affected checks.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('Attack-of-the-Timelout-Attack-of-the-Timelord-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-022923/docs/build-notes.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Two focused engine changes apply','Three focused engine changes apply').replace('2. Fixed-resolution Screen sizing permits fractional downscaling when the viewport is smaller than the logical canvas. The unmodified minimum1 cropped1066×600 on small screens. Native pointer mapping, letterboxing and collision coordinates now remain aligned. Default scaling is Fill.','2. Fixed-resolution Screen sizing permits fractional downscaling when the viewport is smaller than the logical canvas. The unmodified minimum1 cropped1066×600 on small screens. A rounding epsilon keeps fit margins stable. Native pointer mapping, letterboxing and collision coordinates now remain aligned. Default scaling is Fill.\\\\n3. Shell same-name refresh preserves focus before replacing its screen record. Without this, controller character pickers jumped back to the first button after every edit.').replace('The canonical world never reads DOM, draws or plays audio.','The canonical world never reads DOM, draws or plays audio. A separate monotonic network clock catches up fixed steps independently of rendering and local shell pause, and sampled input expires after350ms.');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Final verification pass in progress\n- All game features, menus, independent network clock, sticky assisted records and final credits/feedback are implemented. Root HTML rebuilt at1431KiB with final interview data; exit-interview.json synchronized.\n- State23/23, engine8/8, network18/18. Audio27/27. Browser final suite122 checks (affected49 and38 passed after last fixes). OfficialHub4/4 and real packagedWebRTC15/15 previously passed; final suite adds two input-freshness/no-render checks.\n- Independent network clock is now production behavior, not a test bypass. Local sampled input expires350ms and is cleared on focus/controller loss. Public signaling transiently timed out but real data links succeeded after retry.\n- Final quiet all-suite run currently running in exec session17834. Poll with write_stdin; logs only at end. Expected total234 if all groups complete. Correct any reported failures before delivery.\n- Final docs: README, research, authoring, build-notes, audio, network, verification. Finding ledger26 issues:10 test/visual,16 focused review;5 potentially game breaking. All fixed.\n- Contact sheet: test-artifacts/browser-contact-sheet.png/.html,12 genuine screenshots. Need refresh after final browser screenshot run if desired with tests/contact-sheet.py.\n- Remaining only: inspect all-suite result, record artifact hash/final counts, final progress update and final reply with required Source Information and all ordered feedback answers. Do not modify runtime after testing without rebuild and affected checks.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
